{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Keeping kindness.</b> That a person does before Him." "<b>To thousands.</b> To two thousand generations." "<b>Iniquity and transgression.</b> עֲוֹנוֹת — these are the intentional sins; פְּשָׁעִים — these are the rebellions that a person does to provoke." "<b>And will by no means clear.</b> According to its plain sense, it means He does not forgive the iniquity entirely, but exacts payment from him little by little. And our Sages interpreted: He clears those who repent, and does not clear those who do not repent (Yoma 6)." "<b>Visiting the iniquity of fathers upon children.</b> When they hold the deeds of their fathers in their hands — as He has already explained in another verse: לְשֹׂנְאָי (Exodus 20)." "<b>And unto the fourth generation.</b> The fourth generation. Thus the measure of goodness exceeds the measure of punishment five-hundredfold — for in the measure of goodness He says ״נֹצֵר חֶסֶד לָאֲלָפִים״ (Tosefta Sotah 4)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:33.010740131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}